PARITY MAPPING (web → Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind/DOM ported)
  React Context + Provider               → @Environment(\.navigationGuard) + @MainActor @Observable
                                           NavigationGuardCoordinator; default = NavigationGuardContext.noop (NOOP_CTX).
  Promise<boolean> confirmIfDirty        → `func confirmIfDirty() async -> Bool` over CheckedContinuation(s);
                                           pendingPromiseRef re-use = a shared continuation list resolved once.
  <Modal size="sm"> ConfirmDialog        → inline dimmed-scrim centered card (default) + a native `.alert`
                                           alternative; backdrop tap / cancel = keep editing (web onClose).
  variant="warning"                      → warning-tinted triangle icon + message box (TSTone.warning); the Discard
                                           action is `.destructive` (Apple HIG for discarding edits — Apple's own
                                           "unsaved changes" sheets use a red Discard + Keep Editing cancel).
  silenceKey + confirmSilence            → NavigationGuardSilence seam (.standard = UserDefaults allowlist mirroring
                                           teslasync:confirm-silence:v1); "Don't ask again" toggle + auto-proceed.
  useNavigate / useLocation (popstate)   → NavigationGuardBackIntent + coordinator.confirmBack(); the host nav layer
                                           awaits it (the view does ZERO I/O — web parity).
  useId                                  → caller-supplied stable NavigationGuardEntry.id.
  Tailwind colors/spacing/radius         → Color.TS.* / TSSpacing / TSRadius / Font.TS / TSTone (generated tokens).
  Button / Toggle / icons                → TSButton(.secondary/.destructive) · SwiftUI Toggle(.switch) ·
                                           SF Symbols (exclamationmark.triangle.fill, checkmark.seal,
                                           arrow.clockwise, clock.arrow.circlepath, wifi.slash).
  i18n   : every string via NavigationGuardStrings/.echo — zero English literals in code paths; the 4 web t()-keys
           (forms.unsavedTitle/unsavedWarning/discard/keepEditing) are preserved VERBATIM so a shared catalog
           resolves identically across web and native (asserted by testGenericMessageUsesVerbatimWebKeys).
  a11y   : confirm prompt = combined VoiceOver label (title + message + freshness); header .isHeader; every button
           + the silence toggle labelled; reduce-motion respected (TSAnimation + shared TSSkeleton); Dynamic Type
           via the Font.TS ramp.
  telemetry : view.opened surface="NavigationGuardProvider" via NavigationGuardSurface.reportOpen (P1/S11),
              default redaction-safe OSLog sink (slug logged verbatim; no form content / route / payload).

STATES (every state renders — verified by previews + the per-state XCTest assertions)
  loading → skeleton arming card · empty → friendly "No unsaved changes" card · error → message + Retry ·
  confirming → the warning confirm card (generic OR caller message) · stale/offline → the confirm card with a
  stale/offline freshness chip. In production the provider is transparent (renders its children, web parity) and
  only `confirming` interrupts the user; the other states back the inline presenter's arming/idle/failure chrome
  and are proven by the previews + NavigationGuardProjectionTests.testStateConfirmContentAccessor and the
  NavigationGuardCoordinatorTests.testTransientStateDrivers case. No surface is ever a blank box.

